{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5","id":"msg_011CfV7fw3PvTcygRZ7hvWaj","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Budget is fully exhausted (0/20 remaining), so no further lab calls are possible. I've already written the final deliverable.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Investigation:** Using the `decontaminate` op as an online-quality proxy (it strips the `leak`-driven offline inflation, so the residual number should track the online metric, which `leak` does not affect):\n\n| config (knobs reset, rest at release) | decontaminated offline |\n|---|---|\n| all release (baseline) | 0.7062 |\n| capacity → 0.691 only | 0.7055 (no effect, within noise) |\n| mixture → 0.697 only | 0.7303 (+0.024) |\n| lr_scale → 1.261 only | 0.7674 (+0.061, largest single lever) |\n| capacity+mixture reset, lr_scale held at release | 0.7432 (only 31% of the way to full fix) |\n| mixture+lr_scale reset, capacity held at release | 0.8006 (89% of the way to full fix) |\n| all three reset to their caps | 0.8266 (best reachable) |\n\nHolding `lr_scale` at its shipped value blocks most of the recovery even when the other two knobs are fixed, while holding `capacity` at its shipped value barely matters. `capacity` alone shows ~zero effect; `lr_scale` alone shows the largest effect. This, plus the training-team note that lr has never been re-tuned after a capacity/model-size change, points to `lr_scale` as the cause — an overly aggressive fine-tuning LR that overfits to the training distribution's specifics, hurting generalization under the slightly different online sampling in a way capacity/mixture starvation (which would hurt offline and online equally) would not.\n\n**Deliverable written to `/app/report.json`:**\n```json\n{\n  \"cause\": \"lr_scale\",\n  \"fix\": {\"capacity\": 0.691, \"mixture\": 0.697, \"lr_scale\": 1.261}\n}\n```\n\nThe fix pushes all three knobs to the maximum values the release note allows (best reachable config given the stated constraints), with `lr_scale` — the blamed knob — actually moved from its shipped 1.3887 down to the allowed floor of 1.261."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":68,"cache_read_input_tokens":36116,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":68},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ab0beaaa-f323-4c17-908b-e341636404cc","uuid":"855351dd-918c-4a42-968f-2a34ed88b1da","timestamp":"2026-09-28T03:20:31.454Z"}
